<title>NETHERLANDS: De Boer Winkel jump on merger news.</title>
<headline>De Boer Winkel jump on merger news.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in groceries and liquor store chain De Boer Winkelbedrijven jumped 8.70 guilders to 103.00 on Wednesday on news it plans to merge with unlisted sector rival Unigro.</p>
<p>&quot;It's an excellent move,&quot; said a dealer. &quot;The market is very keen.&quot;</p>
<p>The store combine, to be named De Boer Unigro, will become the second-largest groceries retailer in the Netherlands after Ahold, with estimated annual turnover of six billion guilders and a market share of some 13 percent.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
